WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.281
Word-for-word translation sounds strange.

2
00:00:03.281 --> 00:00:05.734
Translate the meaning instead.

3
00:00:06.074 --> 00:00:08.109
Read the whole sentence first.

4
00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:09.316
Write it the way a

5
00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:10.919
native speaker would.

6
00:00:10.919 --> 00:00:12.735
Then check nothing is lost:

7
00:00:12.735 --> 00:00:13.870
numbers, names,

8
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.273
and negatives.

9
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:16.891
If there's an idiom,

10
00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:18.420
find a matching one.

11
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.342
If there isn't,

12
00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:21.522
just say the meaning plainly.

13
00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:24.489
Government press releases often come

14
00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:25.897
in two languages.

15
00:00:25.897 --> 00:00:28.011
Compare them to practise.

16
00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:29.626
Your turn.

17
00:00:29.626 --> 00:00:31.898
What's the best translation?
